# .publication-denylist — D8 choice (a): publication-safe pattern notation.
# Per-repo D8 ruling recorded: https://github.com/caty-ai/alpha-nightshift/issues/46
# Format: NAME<TAB>REGEX (Python re, IGNORECASE). One rule per line.
#
# D8-(a) notation, following templates/publication-gate/fixtures/sample.publication-denylist
# (`acme[-_ ]secret`): a character class splits each protected literal, so this
# committed file does not itself publish the strings it protects, while the regex
# still matches them. The checker path-excludes this file from its own scan, so it
# is structurally unable to catch a violation here — tests/test_publication_denylist.sh
# is what actually enforces it (issue #50).
#
# Every rule is split, with no exceptions: "no rule may match this file" is a cheap
# mechanical invariant, and an exception list would be the thing that rots. (The
# account slug is separately published in the clear by .github/risk-reviewers.txt,
# which the Risk Review Gate requires — splitting it here costs nothing either way.)
#
# Scope: repo-specific protected literals only — generic secret shapes (tokens,
# private-key blocks) are gitleaks' job (PR-range caller + the pre-flip full-history
# sweep), and duplicating them here would flag the guard tests' deliberate fixtures.
HOME_ABS_PATH	/Users/[a-z0-9_-]+/
# Personal-account references in every shape that carries a locator — after an
# @ or / (handles, scp remotes, social profile paths) or before / . @ (repo refs,
# blog hosts, email local-parts). The bare ID alone is allowed, because
# .github/risk-reviewers.txt must name it by contract (issue #50). The checker's
# own --account-slug backstop only sees github.com / gist / <slug>.github.io, so
# everything else here is uncovered without this rule (seat findings, PR #51).
PERSONAL_ACCOUNT_REF	(?:(?<=[@/])shojikumar[u](?![A-Za-z0-9-])|(?<![A-Za-z0-9-])shojikumar[u][/.@])
FAMILY_VAULT_PATH	SharedHub/famil[y][-_]vault
ALPHA_WIKI_PATH	claude-workspace/alph[a][-_]wiki
TAILSCALE_CGNAT_IP	\b100\.(6[4-9]|[7-9][0-9]|1[01][0-9]|12[0-7])\.[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\b
HANDOFF_DIR	_handoff[s]/
